<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Caris LeVert Paid $14.81m?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>LeVert is paid <strong>$14.81m</strong> because a guard who creates his own shot off the bench is worth the mid-level exception, and he has been paid at roughly that level for six years.</p>
<ul>
<li>Brooklyn extended him at <strong>$52.5m</strong> over three years in 2019 before he had started a full season.</li>
<li>He was paid between <strong>$14m</strong> and <strong>$18.8m</strong> in each of the last seven seasons.</li>
<li><a href="/teams/cleveland-cavaliers/">Cleveland</a> paid him <strong>$32m</strong> across two seasons without him starting most of them.</li>
<li>He has been traded four times inside contracts.</li>
<li>He has played for six clubs in eleven seasons.</li>
</ul>
<p>His salary has sat inside a <strong>$5m</strong> band for seven straight seasons.</p>

